title: Definition 4
---
order: 4
---
short_label: X.Def.III.4
---
statement: Again, if the square on the whole is greater than the square on the annex by the square on a straight line incommensurable with the whole, then, if the whole is commensurable in length with the rational straight line set out, let the apotome be called a <i>fourth apotome</i>;
---
group: defX.III
---
subsection: III
---
body:

